# Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) Project

A clean, modular Python project for performing end-to-end EDA on any tabular dataset.

## 📁 Project Structure

```
eda_project/
├── eda_analysis.py      ← Main script (run this)
├── data_loader.py       ← Load CSV / Excel / synthetic data
├── visualizations.py    ← All plotting functions
├── stats_tests.py       ← Normality, T-test, ANOVA, Chi-square
├── requirements.txt     ← Dependencies
└── README.md
```

## 🚀 Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 2. Run the full EDA pipeline
python eda_analysis.py
```

## 📦 What It Does

| Step | Task |
|------|------|
| 1 | Load dataset (CSV / Excel / synthetic) |
| 2 | Basic info — shape, dtypes, duplicates |
| 3 | Descriptive statistics |
| 4 | Missing value handling (median fill) |
| 5 | Outlier detection (IQR + Z-score) |
| 6 | Correlation matrix |
| 7 | Normality test (Shapiro-Wilk) |
| 8 | Feature engineering |
| 9 | Visualizations → saved as PNG |

## 🔧 Use Your Own Dataset

```python
# In eda_analysis.py, change:
df = load_data()                    # synthetic data
# to:
df = load_data("your_file.csv")    # your CSV
```

